version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-10"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23279014"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AutoDrops/asm-eval"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Evaluation results and a standalone scoring script for ASM, a compact state memory for long-running LLM agents
  (implementation not included). On the internal closed set c3 (216 questions per method) ASM scored 85.6% vs 72.7%
  for full history with about 12.6x less context (context measurements reported from private run logs,
  not reproducible from released data). On a 100-question stratified subset of the LongMemEval ORACLE
  variant (not the official 500-question result) ASM scored 49% vs 58% for BM25 and 66% for full history.
  Preliminary study, not independently reproduced. No LongMemEval dialogues or conversation histories are redistributed;
  the labels file contains IDs, types and reader answers derived from LongMemEval under MIT,
  not CC BY 4.0 (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). Released labels and scenario counts reproduce the
  accuracy and paired statistics described in README; private run-log measurements are excluded.
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - long-term memory
  - evaluation
  - LongMemEval
